  "export": {
    "format": "PNG",
    "transparency": true,
    "recommended_filter": "nearest_neighbor",
    "recommended_scale_factors": [2, 3, 4],
    "facteur": 2,
    "note_facteur": "game pixels × facteur = atlas pixels; 2 → 32 px tiles (tools/construire_atlas.py)",
    "naming_convention": "snake_case",
    "directory_structure": "frontend/public/sprites/{category}/{asset_name}/"
  },
  "notes": [
    "`size` is the target size in game pixels; the generated sprites are about 3 to 5 times larger and not on an exact grid, so they must be downscaled (nearest neighbor) and cleaned up.",
    "`source.sprites` are the numbers of the files cut by `tools/decouper_sprites.py --auto` (see decoupe/planche_01/apercu.png); re-cutting the sheet with different settings may renumber them.",
    "Devices, sensors and tanks were generated on semi-transparent white squares: remove the residual haze when cleaning up.",
    "Keep animation frames aligned to a consistent grid to avoid visual jitter.",
    "Use nearest-neighbor scaling to preserve crisp pixel edges."
  ]
}
